  abstract = {This letter proposes an improved hybrid flux observer (HFO) for sensorless control scheme of permanent magnet synchronous motor (PMSM). The proposed method is robust against stator resistance mismatch, which is the primary factor affecting the performance of the observer at low speed. An compensation angle has been added to the correction part of the current model and voltage model in HFO, in order to reduce errors in the q-axis direction introduced by stator resistance mismatch. The proposed method modifies the characteristic matrix of the observer, resulting in a larger stable operating speed range and better load-carrying capability. Stability proof and parameter tuning method based on small-signal method is also provided. With only one parameter requiring design, the proposed sensorless scheme is simple to implement. The effectiveness of this method is verified by experiments on a 1.0-kW SPMSM (Surface PMSM) drive platform and a 5.2-kW IPMSM (Interior PMSM) drive platform, demonstrating its good generality.},
